// Manifest of canonical ORACLE `.dmevent.ron` files (BL-82 EM-4.9 follow-up,
// data-driven-content cleanup).
//
// Schema: `OracleEventManifest` in
// bevy/xindeler-oracle-host/src/oracle_manifest.rs. Consumed by
// `xindeler_sim_bridge::oracle::ServerOraclePlugin`'s
// `request_well_known_events_from_manifest` system, which requests an
// `AssetServer` handle for every listed bare filename (relative to the
// `oracle://` watch directory) once this manifest loads — required so a
// LATER human/ORACLE write of that exact path is noticed by `bevy_asset`'s
// file watcher (see that module's own doc comment for why an outstanding
// handle is a hard requirement, not a nicety).
//
// Adding a new canonical event to this list is a DATA change: drop the new
// name below, no Rust code change or recompile needed. This is deliberately
// a fixed, explicit list (v1 scope) — a general "scan the whole oracle://
// directory" watcher is a nicer v2, tracked as a deferred follow-up in
// `xindeler_sim_bridge::oracle`'s module doc.
(
    event_filenames: [
        "mist_bound.dmevent.ron",
    ],
)
